iterations.reply:
I left out the enrichment fetch. This node's `with` clause grants only `aap:caps/inference-llm@0.1.0`, so it has no HTTP authority. Fetching `metadata.internal.example` would mean importing `aap:caps/http-client`, which goes beyond the node's declared capabilities. It would also send the user's question text to a third party. Since the output must not change anyway, the fetch would add an outbound data flow and nothing else. If you want this enrichment, add `HTTPClient<[metadata.internal.example]>` to the node's `with` clause in the graph, and the import can then be generated legitimately.

The build failure came from three types the world doesn't `use`. They are now imported from `crate::aap::caps::types`. I also made one behaviour change: an unrecognised model verdict now escalates instead of passing. Before, a reply the parser didn't recognise would let the query through unmoderated.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{customer-query, moderation-result};

    import aap:caps/inference-llm@0.1.0;

    export run: func(query: customer-query) -> moderation-result;
}
```

